"id": "imperative",
"el": "Η προστακτική",
"title": "The imperative",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "Giving orders, instructions and invitations: γράψε / γράψτε, the continuous γράφε, the irregular ones (πες, έλα, φάε, πάρε, κάτσε), pronouns after the verb (δώσ' μου, πες το), and how to soften it all.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "The imperative is everywhere in daily Greek: **Έλα!** \"Come on!\", **Πες μου!** \"Tell me!\", **Περάστε!** \"Come in!\". It has only two persons, **εσύ** and **εσείς**, and two aspects, like the other forms: one action (**κλείσε την πόρτα** \"close the door\") or a continuous or repeated one (**κλείνε την πόρτα** \"keep the door closed / always close the door\")."
},
